Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer* role at *Salesforce*. At Sperse, I architected and delivered a scalable multi-agent CRM platform with Python, LangGraph, LangChain, and FastAPI that securely routes customer requests across 40+ specialized agents for more than 10,000 users. That work reflects the outcome I would bring to Salesforce: highly scalable products that customers can trust, understand, and use.

My engineering experience spans architecture, design, implementation, automated testing, and production delivery. I built a React and TypeScript workflow platform with durable Temporal execution so customers could create, resume, and monitor agent workflows; developed a FastMCP server exposing 160+ backend actions with built-in monitoring; and used GitHub Actions CI/CD with OpenTelemetry evaluations to test latency, accuracy, and safety before deployment. I also guided Claude Code and Codex CLI across deployment pipelines, error monitoring, and automated testing. Previously at Qualitest, I applied object-oriented design in Java and Spring Boot to build a cloud-agnostic storage service and orchestrated 100K+ weekly jobs with AWS Step Functions to prevent Lambda timeouts and improve recovery.

I reinforced that evidence-driven approach by building *ProofTrail AI*, a published Python, LangGraph, and LangChain project for truthful job-match analysis. Its five-stage workflow maps requirements to candidate evidence, surfaces unsupported gaps, and rejects uncited claims through a deterministic validation gate. The recruiter-readable CLI produces observable Markdown and JSON reports, while 15 tests at 99% coverage, strict type checks, linting, and GitHub Actions CI verify the system. This project demonstrates how I use agentic tools, telemetry, and metrics while keeping quality and trust central to delivery.

Salesforce's mission to help companies connect with their customers resonates with the CRM systems I build, and its values of trust, customer success, and innovation match how I approach AI-enabled software: secure access, visible behavior, and evidence-backed release decisions. I would welcome the opportunity to help deliver stable, scalable features that customers adopt and rely on. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting!

